  <tr>
    <th class="tg-0lax"></th>
    <th class="tg-amwm" colspan="2">Heat</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="tg-amwm">Light</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">Normal</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">Supplementary</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="tg-0lax">Normal</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">{@lightn_heatn@}</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">{@lightn_heats@}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="tg-0lax">Supplementary</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">{@lights_heatn@}</td>
    <td class="tg-0lax">\(?\)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<br>

Calculate the expected value of the \(?\) if:

<br>
a) There is no interaction between heat and light
[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]
<br>
<br>
[[feedback:prt1]]
<br>
b) Increased heat and light combined has no added benefit over increased heat on it's own (negative interaction)
[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]
<br>
<br>
[[feedback:prt2]]
<br>
Give a possible value of the \(?\) if:
<br>
<br>
c) Increased heat and light combined has a bigger effect than either on their own (positive interaction)
[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]
[[feedback:prt3]]]]></text>
    </questiontext>
